The clickable card div should have a role="button" attribute and keyboard navigation support (tabIndex={0}, onKeyDown handler) to ensure accessibility for keyboard users. Interactive elements that are not semantic buttons or links need these attributes for proper accessibility.
```suggestion
                className={cardClassName}
                role="button"
                tabIndex={0}
                onClick={() => navigation.handleClick(row)}
                onKeyDown={(event) => {
                  if (event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' ') {
                    event.preventDefault();
                    navigation.handleClick(row);
                  }
                }}
```

The truncated badge should include a title attribute with the full stage value to ensure users can see the complete text on hover or via screen readers when the text is truncated. This is especially important for long stage names that exceed the 140px max-width.
```suggestion
                        className={`text-xs shrink-0 max-w-[140px] truncate ${stageBadgeColor(String(row[stageCol.accessorKey]))}`}
                        title={String(row[stageCol.accessorKey])}
```
